# Swift / SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj
# Alternate scratch paths. The CLT and swiftly toolchains cannot share a build cache, so
# `--scratch-path` is routine here (AGENTS.md "Toolchain + testing"), and red-proofs spawn
# throwaway ones per mutant. Ignored BY CLASS rather than by enumerating `.build-swiftly/`:
# three such dirs showed up untracked from one review round alone.
.build-*/

# OMC runtime / session state (machine-local; never commit)
.omc/

# In-repo per-domain worktrees (each a checkout of a feature branch)
.worktrees/

# Session scratchpads may contain raw oracle output; ignore by class if one is misplaced here.
scratchpad/

# Ephemeral session-handoff brief — MUST NEVER be committed
START-HERE.md

# Live test-cleanup log (machine-local run state; lists created test items to delete)
TEST-CLEANUP.md

# PII-bearing artifacts — NEVER commit real Apple data into this public repo. Golden-JSON
# snapshots MUST be synthetic and may be committed; live dumps go under live-dumps/.
*.eml
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.abcddb
*.log
.env
.env.*
live-dumps/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Note: Package.resolved IS committed (this is an executable, so we pin deps).
PARITY-TEST-MATRIX.md
MAIL-PARITY-AUDIT-*.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
NONMAIL-PARITY-AUDIT-*.json
MAIL-PARITY-WORKLIST-*.json

# Live-run audit artifacts — generated by running the CLI/MCP against REAL accounts,
# so they contain real contacts, addresses, subjects and account structure. Ignored BY
# CLASS, not by enumerating known filenames: the D9 live-audit dump
# was committed and pushed precisely because it did not match any of the by-name patterns
# below it (see HUMAN-DECISIONS.md D9). Any new live-run dump must match one of these.
docs/parity-*
*-AUDIT-*.json
*-RECONCILIATION-*
*-reconciliation-*
live-dumps/

# `npm install` in the notes-markdown-oracle fixture (regenerating goldens) drops these in
# the repo; the generator is committed, its dependency tree is not.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
.omx/

# Root-level briefs BY CLASS, not by name. Any root-level *.md that is not explicitly
# un-ignored below is invisible to every form of `git add` — including `git add .` and
# `git add <dir>`, which DO sweep untracked files. This is the technical control behind the
# "session-handoff briefs live outside the repo" rule in AGENTS.md: a brief that lands here
# under an arbitrary name (a gap.md, a paste of live findings) cannot be staged by accident.
# Same by-class reasoning as the audit-dump patterns above. Adding a legitimate new root
# document means adding its negation here, deliberately.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/HUMAN-DECISIONS.md
